cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CenGeometry: a geometric and mechanical model of the centriole cross-section"
message: "If you use this tool or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hatzopoulos
    given-names: Georgios
    affiliation: UPGON
repository-code: "https://github.com/UPGON/CenGeometry"
abstract: >-
  A geometric and mechanical model of the centriole cross-section. One
  repeating unit is represented as rigid bodies joined by connections that
  can rotate; because the units must close into a ring, the model solves for
  the least-strained arrangement that still fits together. It predicts how
  structural perturbations -- SAS-6 mutations that change cartwheel symmetry,
  altered coiled-coil lengths, loss of the C-tubule -- change the architecture
  of the whole organelle. Every dimension is measured from a cryo-ET-derived
  schematic by a re-runnable calibration script.
keywords:
  - centriole
  - cartwheel
  - SAS-6
  - microtubule triplet
  - A-C linker
  - structural modelling
  - cryo-ET
references:
  - type: software
    title: "centriole.m: parametric centriole cross-section (original MATLAB script)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Neves
        given-names: Aitana
    notes: >-
      The original script this project grew from, kept in legacy/ for
      provenance. Superseded by the Python model but its ancestor.
